		DeathText: {
			01: The dodgeroll makes you immune to attacks. Mastering it is necessary for survival!
			02: Glowing green skulls hold important secrets...Right Click to open them
			03: The dodgeroll keybind can be changed in Controls. Recommended Controls can be turned on via Mod Config: Controls.
			04: Crystal shards often hint at secrets, chests or hidden paths nearby...
			05: Losing souls on death can be disabled in the config.
			06: Check the description of your items to see if any can be upgraded with Dark Souls
			07: Teal Pressure Pads can only be activated with small projectiles
			08: If you can do something, you're intended to! Be clever, and use 'cheap' tricks to gain every advantage
			09: Using potions during normal combat is often necessary to survive
			PermaPot: Permanent potions need special crystals, but normal shards can be refined into them
			10: You can dodge mid-air to avoid attacks, cross longer gaps and reverse your momentum instantly...
			11: Get a bad modifier on a weapon? Talk to Jade, the Emerald Herald, outside Ashenpeak Village. She can remove it with her Blessing
			12: If you feel lost, seek the dark places on your map. There are secrets and paths in almost every direction
			13: Soapstones offer many important hints
			14: Use the Guide Slot in your inventory to easily see what your loot can be transformed into
			15: Hitting enemies with the tip of a whip will deal extra damage
			16: Lao Tzu: "Let your workings remain a mystery. Just show people the results."
			PermaPot2: Some perma potions can be strengthened, and eventually surpass their normal variants.
			17: Some vanilla recipes have been removed. You must find these items in the world by exploring
			18: Item tooltips often have information vital to your survival...
			19: You may encounter bosses before you can defeat them. If in doubt, come back when you're stronger
			20: Welcome to the Dark Souls of Terraria
			21: Grey Stone Gates cannot be broken and must be opened by a lever or switch
			22: The Chloranthy Ring massively improves your dodgeroll, allowing superior evasion...
			23: Enemies in certain dark areas drop Humanity, which can reroll curse stats
			24: Need more advice? Join the discord, and get tips without even needing to die for them.
			25: Progression clues can be found by hovering over entries in the Boss Hunting Tome, or some unique items dropped by bosses
			26: Remember to dodgeroll
			27: If you go above 100% crit chance you have a chance to multicrit, allowing you to deal even more damage
			GoodLuck: You've now seen almost every death tip, but your journey is nowhere near over. Good luck, we hope you enjoy it!
			Poem:
				'''
				You're bad, 
				     you're mad,
				     cope, seethe and mald,
				     until you're bald.
				'''
			WallDeathReason: " was consumed by The Wall of Flesh"
			BotC1: Bearer of the Curse mode can be disabled at any time...
			BotC2: Bearer of the Curse mode is intended for experienced players
			BotC3: Try reading the Darksign's description
			IWantToRemoveThisCaptainObviousShit: Avoid getting hit by enemy attacks
			TotallyNotMeantToBeToxic: Get Good :)
			HeavyRoll: Heavy roll you got there!
			BossDeath1: Don't give up! Some bosses might take several tries to defeat
			BossDeath2: Certain bosses can be fought earlier than necessary. If you're struggling, try coming back when you're more powerful
			DarkCloud: You can't outrun your shadow
			Tonberry: (O_O;)
			Marilith: Some powerful attacks can only be avoided by dodgerolling!
			ChloranthyRingTip: The Chloranthy Ring massively improves your dodgeroll, allowing even more evasion...
			Tip: "Tip: "
		}

		Events: {
			Pinwheel: Pinwheel turns its glance to you.
			Death: The fated day of your death has arrived.
			QueenSlime: Queen Slime emerges from her Hallowed cave!
			GreatRedKnightInvasion: A Great Red Knight has invaded your world!
			GoblinShark: A Hemogoblin Shark is thirsty for blood!
			SkeletronPrimeRemix: Skeletron Prime, the forgotten mech, has awoken!
