			GravemawTome: {
				DisplayName: Gravemaw Tome
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Four spells bound in one tome
					Tap left click: fire a fan of homing soul-skulls
					Hold left click: charge an expanding soul nova
					Tap right click: lob an orb that opens a black hole
					Hold right click: channel an inhaling maw that drains life
					Advanced control option available in Controls config
					'''
				AdvancedTooltip:
					'''
					Four spells bound in one tome
					Aim at or above a point 3 tiles below your feet:
					Tap left click: fire a fan of homing soul-skulls
					Hold left click: charge an expanding soul nova
					Aim more than 3 tiles below your feet:
					Tap left click: lob an orb that opens a black hole
					Hold left click: channel an inhaling maw that drains life
					'''
			}

			JungleFeather: {
				DisplayName: Jungle Feather
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Summons the Jungle Wyvern 
					An ancient beast that once guarded an advanced civilization, 
					long since forgotten. To this day, it watches over the lost 
					city, ripping to shreds any traveler who should discover it.
					'''
				WrongTime: The ancient Jungle Wyvern remains deep in slumber... Retry at night.
				WrongLocation: The ancient Jungle Wyvern must be summoned underground.
				Summon: "A rumbling thunder shakes the ground below you... "
			}

			LostScrollOfGwyn: {
				DisplayName: Lost Scroll of Gwyn
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Used to summon Gwyn, Lord of Cinder. 
					Gwyn may prove impossible to defeat unless you have defeated 7 guardians of the Abyss:
					Artorias, Seath, the Lich King, Kraken, Marilith, the Blight, and the Wyvern Mage Shadow. 
					Only the true warrior of the age will survive this fight. 
					'''
				Summon: "Defeat me, and you shall inherit the fire of this world... "
			}

			MindCube: {
				DisplayName: Mind Cube
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Summons Attraidies, the Mindflayer King 
					This is it. The final battle. 
					[c/ffbf00:To find the light and dark shards needed to craft this in adventure mode... Seek the Dark Tower of Attraidies.]
					[c/00ffd4:If you are in the Remix map, you should also look for the Old One's Tree in the jungle...]
					'''
			}

			MindflayerIllusionRelic: {
				DisplayName: Mindflayer Illusion Relic
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Use this relic to summon the final battle with Attraidies. 
					Attraidies laughs. '[c/ff08ff:Alright Red, I'm content to end this now. Face me. No more games.]'
					'''
			}

			PottedPlanteraBulb: {
				DisplayName: Potted Plantera Bulb
				Tooltip: Summons Plantera
			}

			SerrisBait: {
				DisplayName: Serris Bait
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Attracts and Summons Serris, An ancient alien who crash-landed in the desert centuries ago.
					Given his dangerous nature and unique properties, he was imprisoned by Attraidies
					beneath the tower and also used to create some advanced technologies.
					'''
			}

			StoneOfSeath: {
				DisplayName: Stone of Seath
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Summons Seath the Scaleless, a great dragon granted the title of Duke by Lord Gwyn for his 
					assistance in defeating the Everlasting Dragons and given a fragment of a Lord Soul. Seath 
					was driven insane during his research on the Scales of Immortality, which he could never 
					obtain. Ironically, he is now an immortal himself, a true Undead by means of his research 
					into the Primordial Crystal, which he stole from the dragons when he defected.
					'''
				Summon: "Thy death will only fuel my immortality, Red... "
			}

			MasterRing: {
				DisplayName: Master Ring
				Tooltip:
					'''
					This ring leads to damnation for those tempted by its treacherous and evil power.
					Summons the Witchking who will answer the call of the ring.
					'''
			}

			TomeOfSlograAndGaibon: {
				DisplayName: Tome of Slogra and Gaibon
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Summons the nocturnal beast known as Slogra, a reptilian creature who fights alongside the demon 
					known as Gaibon. Not much is known of Gaibon, though it is legend that Slogra was once a man,  
					whose rings he wore finally consumed him until the man was gone and only his lost soul remained
					'''
			}

			WateryEgg: {
				DisplayName: Watery Egg
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Summons The Sorrow 
					Must be used near the ocean
					'''
				WrongLocation: You can only use this in the Ocean.
			}

			WingOfTheFallen: {
				DisplayName: Wing of the Fallen
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Summons the Wyvern Mage, a powerful demon adept with the forces of magic and lightning
					The Wyvern Mage is known to command the loyalty of a fiery Wyvern with white scales as strong as steel
					If you cannot defeat the Wyvern Mage after several tries, it would be wise
					to return later when you've become stronger and possess greater abilities.
					'''
				WrongTime: The Wyvern Mage is not present in this dimension... Retry at night.
				Summon: "It was a mistake to summon me... "
			}

			WingOfTheGhostWyvern: {
				DisplayName: Wing of the Ghost Wyvern
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Frees the Wyvern Mage's Shadow from its Glass Prison.
					The Wyvern Mage once created a shadow form of himself, cursed by the powers of the Abyss
					It was so hideous that the Mage imprisoned his shadow self in a massive glass cage, enchanted by dark magic
					'''
				WrongTime: The Ghost Wyvern is not present in this dimension... Retry at night.
				Summon: You think death is the end? You haven't begun to understand my powers, Red...
			}

			BossRematchTome: {
				DisplayName: Boss Hunting Tome
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Hover over any boss in the menu for a hint on where to find it
					Allows you to re-summon any boss you have defeated
					Left click to show Boss Select Menu, then click on the Boss icon to summon
					Use the arrows on both sides to switch between different periods
					Bosses summoned in this way will not drop dark souls, guardian souls or stamina vessels
					However, they will drop the rest of their normal loot
					[Developer note: Not all bosses can be summoned this way yet, but the rest will be added over time]
					'''
				None: No rematchable bosses defeated!
				Selected: "Currently selected boss: "
				Forbidden: Can not summon a second boss while one is alive!
				Duo1: Slogra and Gaibon
				Attraidies1: Attraidies First Phase
				Attraidies2: Attraidies Final Form
				Next: Next Boss:
				Location: Where to find:
				DeathCountText: Death Count: {0}
				// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
				//  Clue index → boss mapping. Each clue N corresponds to the boss with NPC.rarity = N.
				//  Hover behavior:
				//    Defeated boss → shows "Next Boss:" + clue (rarity + 1)
				//    Undefeated (???) → shows "Where to find:" + this boss's own clue (rarity)
				//  Undefeated clues are gated by era (pre-hardmode/hardmode/SHM) so end-game bosses
				//  stay hidden until the player has progressed there.
				//
				//  Rarity → boss mapping. Modded bosses set NPC.rarity in their own SetDefaults.
				//  Vanilla bosses get their rarity assigned by tsorcRevamp in NPCs/VanillaChanges.cs
				//  (search "npc.rarity = N" in that file to find/edit). [PHM] = pre-hardmode,
				//  [HM] = hardmode, [SHM] = Super Hard Mode.
				//
				//    1  [PHM] Leonhard               (Special/LeonhardPhase1)             — modded
				//    2  [PHM] Red Knight             (Enemies/RedKnight)                  — modded
				//    3  [PHM] Pinwheel               (Bosses/Pinwheel)                    — modded
				//    4  [PHM] Eye of Cthulhu         (VanillaChanges.cs)                  — vanilla
				//    5  [PHM] Brain of Cthulhu       (VanillaChanges.cs)                  — vanilla
				//    6  [PHM] Eater of Worlds        (VanillaChanges.cs)                  — vanilla
				//    7  [PHM] Ancient Oolacile Demon (Bosses/AncientOolacileDemon)        — modded
				//    8  [PHM] King Slime             (VanillaChanges.cs)                  — vanilla
				//    9  [PHM] Slogra (+ Gaibon)      (Bosses/Slogra)                      — modded
				//   10  [PHM] Queen Bee              (VanillaChanges.cs)                  — vanilla
				//   11  [PHM] Skeletron             (VanillaChanges.cs)                   — vanilla
				//   12  [PHM] Deerclops              (VanillaChanges.cs)                  — vanilla
				//   13  [PHM] Jungle Wyvern          (Bosses/JungleWyvern/JungleWyvernHead) — modded
				//   14  [PHM] Ancient Demon          (Bosses/AncientDemon)                — modded
				//   15  [PHM] Wall of Flesh          (VanillaChanges.cs)                  — vanilla
				//   16  [HM]  Queen Slime            (VanillaChanges.cs)                  — vanilla
				//   17  [HM]  The Rage               (Bosses/TheRage)                     — modded
				//   18  [HM]  Wyvern Mage            (Bosses/WyvernMage/WyvernMage)       — modded
				//   19  [HM]  The Sorrow             (Bosses/TheSorrow)                   — modded
				//   20  [HM]  Serris                 (Bosses/Serris/SerrisX)              — modded
				//   21  [HM]  Death / True Death     (Bosses/Death, Special/TrueDeath)    — modded
				//   22  [HM]  The Hunter             (Bosses/TheHunter)                   — modded
				//   23  [HM]  The Destroyer          (VanillaChanges.cs)                  — vanilla
				//   24  [HM]  The Machine (PrimeV2)  (Bosses/PrimeV2/TheMachine)          — modded
				//   25  [HM]  Plantera               (VanillaChanges.cs)                  — vanilla
				//   26  [HM]  Golem                  (VanillaChanges.cs, GolemHeadFree)   — vanilla
				//   27  [HM]  Empress of Light       (VanillaChanges.cs, HallowBoss)      — vanilla
				//   28  [HM]  Cataluminance          (Bosses/Cataluminance)               — modded
				//   29  [HM]  Attraidies hidden phases (not shown as their own Tome entry)
				//   30  [HM]  Attraidies (Real)      (Bosses/Okiku/FinalForm/Attraidies)  — modded
				//   31  [SHM] Hellkite Dragon        (Bosses/SuperHardMode/HellkiteDragon/HellkiteDragonHead) — modded
				//   32  [SHM] Witchking              (Bosses/SuperHardMode/Witchking)     — modded
				//   33  [SHM] Moon Lord              (VanillaChanges.cs, MoonLordFreeEye) — vanilla
				//   34  [SHM] Water Fiend Kraken     (Bosses/SuperHardMode/Fiends/WaterFiendKraken)   — modded
				//   35  [SHM] Earth Fiend Lich       (Bosses/SuperHardMode/Fiends/EarthFiendLich)     — modded
				//   36  [SHM] Fire Fiend Marilith    (Bosses/SuperHardMode/Fiends/FireFiendMarilith)  — modded
				//   37  [SHM] Blight                 (Bosses/SuperHardMode/Blight)        — modded
				//   38  [SHM] Abysmal Oolacile Sorc. (Bosses/SuperHardMode/AbysmalOolacileSorcerer)   — modded
				//   39  [SHM] Artorias               (Bosses/SuperHardMode/Artorias)      — modded
				//   40  [SHM] Seath the Scaleless    (Bosses/SuperHardMode/Seath/SeathTheScalelessHead) — modded
				//   41  [SHM] Wyvern Mage Shadow     (Bosses/SuperHardMode/GhostWyvernMage/WyvernMageShadow) — modded
				//   42  [SHM] Chaos                  (Bosses/SuperHardMode/Chaos)         — modded (currently has no rarity set; defaults to 0 — fix in its SetDefaults)
				//   43  [SHM] Dark Cloud             (Bosses/SuperHardMode/DarkCloud)     — modded
				//   44  [SHM] Gwyn                   (Bosses/SuperHardMode/Gwyn)          — modded
				//   45        "True ending" message — shown as the "Next Boss" hint when hovering Gwyn
				//   48  [PHM] Vessel of Souls        (presentation-only clue index; progression order 5)
				//
				//  To rebind a clue to a different boss, edit that boss's `NPC.rarity = N` (or the
				//  `npc.rarity = N` line in VanillaChanges.cs for vanilla bosses). To rewrite a clue's
				//  text, just edit the localization line below. Many `*Desc` clues use the shared
				//  Mods.tsorcRevamp.BossChecklist.*Desc strings (defined near the top of this file)
				//  so the Boss Checklist mod UI and the Boss Hunting Tome stay in sync.
				// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
				1: "{$BossChecklist.LeonhardDesc}"
				2: What is under the mountain cave where Leonhard dwells, or at end of the Path of Ambition?
				3: "{$BossChecklist.PinwheelDesc}"
				4: Seek the chilling depths of the Earth Temple, where the fountains pool their waters.
				5: Delve deep inside the Corruption Temple, or investigate rumours about crimson on the surface, to the East.
				6: Seek the Corruption Temple, East of the Arazium Mountain Chasm.
				7: "{$BossChecklist.AncientOolacileDemonDesc}"
				8: Explore the Rainforest of the Orid Tribe, East of your burned house. Gold temple ruins hide a secret.
				9: "{$BossChecklist.SlograAndGaibonDesc}"
				10: From the Underground Jungle Ruins to the Forgotten City, Larvas are everywhere.
				11: Found past the Lake of Flowered Paths, deep in the underground jungle. Open the shut gate.
				12:
					'''
					Check the basement of the Wizard's house.
					Remix Map: Seek far to the East, at the entrance to the Frozen Ocean past the Hallow.
					'''
				13: "{$BossChecklist.JungleWyvernDesc}"
				14: "{$BossChecklist.AncientDemonDesc}"
				15: Past the four gates West of the Fire Temple. Will you find an answer on the altar?
				16: Search the Hallowed Caverns, which have been sealed by Cobalt.
				17: "{$BossChecklist.TheRageDesc}"
				18: "{$BossChecklist.WyvernMageDesc}"
				19: "{$BossChecklist.TheSorrowDesc}"
				20: "{$BossChecklist.SerrisDesc}"
				21: "{$BossChecklist.DeathDesc}"
				22: "{$BossChecklist.TheHunterDesc}"
				23: It awaits at the end of the Shadow Temple, buried under the Western desert.
				24: Below a broken, familiar bridge, you will find a temple flooded to protect villagers from what was sealed inside.
				25:
					'''
					Why do the Great Pyramid and Hunter's arena have the same pink flowers?
					Remix Map: Search in the Jungle Ruins for the entrance to its lush and forgotten depths.
					'''
				26: Where does the Teleporter of the Great Pyramid lead to?
				27: Golem controls the forcefield of the floating island high above Ashen Peak village.
				28: Atop the Twin Peaks of Arazium, find the temple mouth that gazes at the sky above and the Great Chasm Below.
				29: Craft the 8 Crests with shards found at the top of Attraidies' Dark Tower.
				30: "{$BossChecklist.RealAttraidiesDesc}"
				31: "{$BossChecklist.HellkiteDragonDesc}"
				32: "{$BossChecklist.WitchkingDesc}"
				33:
					'''
					Solve the puzzle of Three stone pillars on the West side of the Ashen Cave.
					Remix Map: Confront the four celestial pillars and search for an ancient alien structure in the sky.
					'''
				34: "{$BossChecklist.WaterFiendKrakenDesc}"
				35: "{$BossChecklist.EarthFiendLichDesc}"
				36: "{$BossChecklist.FireFiendMarilithDesc}"
				37: "{$BossChecklist.BlightDesc}"
				38: "{$BossChecklist.AbysmalOolacileSorcererDesc}"
				39: "{$BossChecklist.ArtoriasDesc}"
				40: "{$BossChecklist.SeathTheScalelessDesc}"
				41: "{$BossChecklist.WyvernMageShadowDesc}"
				42: "{$BossChecklist.ChaosDesc}"
				43: "{$BossChecklist.DarkCloudDesc}"
				44: "{$BossChecklist.GwynDesc}"
				45: Congratulations! You have unlocked the true ending of the game!
				46: "{$BossChecklist.OptionalMysteryDesc}"
				47: "{$BossChecklist.OptionalMysteryDesc}"
				48: "{$BossChecklist.VesselOfSoulsDesc}"
			}

			BraveWarriorSoul: {
				DisplayName: Soul of a Brave Warrior
				Tooltip: Consume to gain 5000 souls
			}

			BrokenPicksaw: {
				DisplayName: Broken Picksaw
				Tooltip:
					'''
					An ancient and powerful tool seems to have been stripped for parts. It is too damaged to be repaired
					[c/00ffd4:The remnants have been drained of their power, and quietly hum with Attraidies' dark magic.]
					[c/ffbf00:It seems if you want the power to break Lihzahrd bricks you'll have to take it from him]...
					This item no longer serves any purpose, and should be discarded
					'''
			}

			BrokenDarkMagicRing: {
				DisplayName: Broken Dark Magic Ring
				Tooltip:
					'''
					A dark magic ring, broken into two pieces...
					Miakoda: "To reforge this ring and restore its magical abilitiy,
					you'll need 5 White Titanite and 1000 Dark Souls.
					To find what we need, we should seek out the Evil Biomes and the Dungeon."
					'''
			}

			CharcoalPineResin: {
				DisplayName: Charcoal Pine Resin
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Black charcoal-like pine resin
					Consume to imbue melee weapons with fire({$CommonItemTooltip.SecondDuration})
					Particularly effective against woody enemies
					{$CommonItemTooltip.MeleeWhipDmg@1}
					'''
			}

			AbyssFlask: {
				DisplayName: Flask of the Abyss
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Melee and Whip attacks inflict enemies with Abyssal Inferno
					Increase melee and whip damage and crit by 6%
					'''
			}

			CrestOfCorruption: {
				DisplayName: Crest of Corruption
				Tooltip:
					'''
					A shard of glowing demonite, oozing with phazon
					[c/00ffd4:This one contains a riddle:] 
					"[c/ffbf00:Below a Broken, familiar Bridge, you will find me.]"
					'''
			}

			CrestOfEarth: {
				DisplayName: Crest of Earth
				Tooltip: ""
				AdvMode:
					'''
					A shard of pure minerals
					One of eight. [c/00ffd4:On its side there's a clue:]
					"[c/ffbf00:Two paths lead to my entrance. Below the Oasis in the Desert, Serris unlocks the Way.]
					"[c/ffbf00:In a small sandy Cave atop a hill, a Chlorophyte Gate guards the other.]"
					'''
				RemixMode:
					'''
					A shard of pure minerals
					One of eight. [c/00ffd4:On its side there's a clue:]
					"[c/ffbf00:Two paths lead to my entrance. Deep in the Dark Tower, Serris unlocks the Way.]
					"[c/ffbf00:In a cave in the Mycelium Forest, a Chlorophyte Gate guards the other.]"
					'''
			}

			CrestOfFire: {
				DisplayName: Crest of Fire
				Tooltip:
					'''
					A shard of blazing fury
					You don't know what it's for, but you're sure it's important.
					[c/00ffd4:After defeating The Rage, Miakoda tells you about the Wyvern Mage that lives high atop the mountain above these caverns] - 
					[c/00ffd4:an ally of Attraidies.] [c/ffbf00:"If he is helping the Mindflayer King, he could know where your wife Asha is."]
					'''
			}

			CrestOfLife: {
				DisplayName: Crest of Life
				Tooltip:
					'''
					A shard of woven vine, stronger than iron
					One of eight.
					[c/00ffd4:Threaded between its strands, another riddle:] 
					"[c/ffbf00:You've found the Key. But where is the Lock?]"
					'''
			}

			CrestOfSky: {
				DisplayName: Crests of Sky
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Three shards of oxygenated carbonate
					Combined this makes one of eight.
					When I fit all the pieces together, there's still something missing.
					[c/00ffd4:These crests contains the final riddle:]
					"[c/ffbf00:Towering Heights, Far to the West. The Molten Eye of Attraidies looks to the Sky Above. He is near.]"
					'''
			}

			CrestOfSteel: {
				DisplayName: Crest of Steel
				Tooltip: ""
				AdvMode:
					'''
					A shard of burning hot steel
					One of eight.
					[c/00ffd4:A riddle is etched into the metal:] 
					"[c/ffbf00:Above the Machine's Throne, Below the Dryad's Cove: A Locked Door guards an Ancient Pyramid, long ago forgotten.]"
					'''
				RemixMode:
					'''
					A shard of burning hot steel
					One of eight.
					[c/00ffd4:A riddle is etched into the metal:] 
					"[c/ffbf00:Somewhere in the Jungle, Near the exit of the Volcano: A Chlorophyte Gate guards the entrance to lush, wild depths, long ago forgotten.]"
					'''
			}

			CrestOfStone: {
				DisplayName: Crest of Stone
				Tooltip:
					'''
					A shard of solar-charged masonry
					One of eight.
					[c/00ffd4:A riddle is etched into the stone:]
					"[c/ffbf00:Atop the Twin Peaks of Arazium, we gaze at Sky Above, and the Great Chasm Below. We are the Eyes of the Ancient One.]"
					'''
			}

			CrestOfWater: {
				DisplayName: Crest of Water
				Tooltip:
					'''
					A shard of crystallized water
					A second piece. 'Are these artifacts part of a puzzle?'
					[c/00ffd4:This shard contains a riddle:] "[c/ffbf00:Beneath the Burning hot sun,]
					[c/ffbf00:sheltered from the blistering Western Winds, Black Smoke with a faint Violet Glow illuminates the path.]"
					'''
			}

			CursedSoul: {
				DisplayName: Cursed Soul
				Tooltip: "'The essence of cursed beings from the abyss'"
			}

			Darksign: {
				DisplayName: Darksign
				Tooltip:
					'''
					A talisman of the cycle. Left-click to cycle to the next tier:
					[c/aaaaaa:Classic] → [c/6d8827:Unkindled] → [c/dd3333:Bearer of the Curse] → [c/aaaaaa:Classic]

					[c/6d8827:Unkindled] (default): Estus and Cerulean flasks bound to
					Quick Heal and Quick Mana. Upgrades drop from bosses.
					Healing items work at half strength; mana regen reduced outside bonfires.

					[c/dd3333:Bearer of the Curse]: All Unkindled features plus combat class
					mechanics, an extra accessory slot, and {0}% more souls.
					Weapons drain stamina, healing potions don't work, mana regen is
					disabled outside bonfires, and dying costs {1}% max HP until your
					soul is recovered.

					[c/aaaaaa:Classic]: No flasks. Vanilla Terraria healing and magic systems.

					Right-click to preview class-specific Bearer of the Curse mechanics.
					'''
				Enabled: You have become the Bearer of the Curse
				Disabled: The curse has been lifted
				Unkindled: You rise as the Unkindled — your fire still smolders.
				BearerOfTheCurse: You have taken up the burden — the Curse is yours to bear.
				Classic: You let the flame fade. The curse is lifted.
				State_Classic: "[c/aaaaaa:Currently:] Classic [c/aaaaaa:— click to become] [c/6d8827:Unkindled]"
				State_Unkindled: "[c/6d8827:Currently:] Unkindled [c/aaaaaa:— click to take up the] [c/dd3333:Curse]"
				State_BotC: "[c/dd3333:Currently:] Bearer of the Curse [c/aaaaaa:— click to return to] [c/aaaaaa:Classic]"
				UnkindledCerulean:
					'''
					[c/ea00ea:mana regen bonuses increase total mana restored and mana regen delay penalties increase total mana restoration time.]
					[c/ea00ea:Mana Potions still work and resting at a Bonfire will restore mana, drinking the Cerulean Flask also cures Mana Sickness.]
					'''
				Melee:
					'''
					[c/ff8400:Lethal Tempo: Melee base attack speed is reduced to {0}%.]
					[c/ff8400:Hitting enemies with melee attacks will grant stacks of Lethal Tempo,]
					[c/ff8400:these increase your attack speed temporarily and fall off after a few seconds, if not refreshed.]
					[c/ff8400:Each stack grants {1}% attack speed, up to {2}% at the maximum of {3} stacks.]
					'''
				Summon:
					'''
					[c/6efaff:Conqueror: Summon base damage is reduced to {0}%, but hitting enemies with whips will grant a stack of Conqueror(2 on a tip hit),]
					[c/6efaff:these increase summon damage temporarily and fall off after a few seconds, if not refreshed.]
					[c/6efaff:Each stack grants {1}% damage, up to {2}% at the maximum of {3} stacks.]
					[c/6efaff:At max stacks, gain {4}% Summon Tag Duration.]
					'''
			}

			DarkSoul: {
				DisplayName: Dark Soul
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Soul of a fallen creature.
					Can be used at Demon Altars to forge new weapons, items, and armors.
					'''
			}

			DeadChicken: {
				DisplayName: Dead Chicken
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Can be cooked at a cooking pot
					Cooked chicken heals {0} HP and inflicts only {1} seconds of potion cooldown. Wow! Tasty!
					'''
			}

			DestructionElement: {
				DisplayName: Destruction Element
				Tooltip:
					'''
					Used for making high damage guns
					The strange way it feels warm to the touch reminds you of somewhere...
					'''
			}

			DiamondPickaxe: {
				DisplayName: Diamond Pickaxe
				Tooltip:
					'''
					An ideal pickaxe for exploring...
					The diamond tip has been imbued with magic from a celestial being.
					Because of this, it can do no harm to living creatures, but its tip breaks through blocks
					with incredible ease... In fact, it moves so fast in your hand,
					you can hardly see it, yet using it feels effortless...
					'''
			}

			DisabledRecipe: {
				DisplayName: Disabled Recipe
				Tooltip:
					'''
					This recipe has been disabled!
					You will have to find this item in the world!
					'''
			}

			DisabledSale: {
				DisplayName: Disabled Sale
				Tooltip: This sale has been deemed illegal! As such, I cannot sell it to you.
			}

			GameManual: {
				DisplayName: Game Manual
				Tooltip: ""
				PageHeader: — Page {0} of {1}: {2} —
				Turn: Right-click to turn the page
				TurnAndToggle: Right-click to turn the page · Left-click to toggle Recommended Controls
				Heading1: How to Read This Manual
				Page1:
					'''
					Right-click this book to turn the page. 
					Page 2 explains your extra inventory slots, page 3 explains the controls, and pages 4–11 explain the mod's core mechanics.
					'''
				Heading2: Your Extra Inventory Slots
				Page2:
					'''
					2nd Slot: Equip a second weapon, tool, consumable or shield in this slot and use with right mouse.
					Storage Slot: a bottomless container to keep your inventory uncluttered. Press T to open it from anywhere. Shift-click to transfer items.			
					Guide Slot: drop any item in to see every recipe that uses it.
					Souls Slot: Your Dark Souls collect here automatically.					
					'''
				Heading3: Controls
				Page3:
					'''
					Recommended Controls rebinds several keys at once to a layout built for this mod.
					The dodge roll and other mod-specific actions can be rebound via Settings: Controls.
					Your Estus Flask is bound to Quick Heal, and the Cerulean Tear to Quick Mana.
					'''
				Heading4: The 2nd Slot
				Page4:
					'''
					It takes weapons without a right-click function, throwables, consumables, tools and shields.
					Accessories cannot be equipped in the slot.
					Shields are the exception. They also keep their full passive effects,
					exactly as if worn in an accessory slot, which frees that slot for something else.
					Right mouse priority: your held weapon's alt-fire, then this slot, then an equipped shield.
					'''
				Heading5: Stamina
				Page5:
					'''
					Attacking, dodge rolling and blocking all spend stamina.
					Run out and you cannot attack or roll until some comes back.
					Stamina Vessels found throughout the world raise your maximum permanently.
					'''
				Heading6: Dodge Rolling
				Page6:
					'''
					Rolling costs stamina and makes you briefly invulnerable.
					Learn the timing and you can pass straight through an attack.
					Rolling in the air allows you to cross bigger gaps and reverse your momentum instantly.
					A perfect dodge refunds half its cost and briefly boosts stamina regen and critical strike chance.
					'''
				Heading7: Estus, Cerulean and Bonfires
				Page7:
					'''
					The Estus Flask heals and the Cerulean Tear restores mana. Both hold limited charges.
					Rest at a bonfire to refill every charge and set your respawn point.
					Bonfires also let you warp to any other bonfire you already lit.
					Estus Flask Shards add charges. Sublime Bone Dust makes each charge stronger.
					'''
				Heading8: Dark Souls
				Page8:
					'''
					Dark Souls are your currency, gathered from everything you kill.
					Look for items labeled as a "Dark Souls recipe material" and place in the Guide slot to see what you can make. 
					Craft souls into new items at bonfires and demon altars, or convert them into soul coins to buy items from shop keepers.
					When you die you drop every soul you are carrying and leave a bloodstain where you fell. 
					Return to it to take them all back — but die again before you reach it and they are gone for good.					
					This can be turned off in the mod's config if you would rather not lose them.
					Dropped souls survive save & reload.
					'''
				Heading9: Finding Your Way
				Page9:
					'''
					The Emerald Herald will give you the Boss Hunting Tome.
					Hovering over any undiscovered boss in its menu offers a clue for where that boss is found,
					which is the best way to work out where to go next when you are lost. 
					Glowing red = next required major boss. Purple = optional major boss. Orange = optional great boss. Yellow = optional field boss.
					Clues for optional bosses and the next required boss is unlocked by defeating the current required boss. 
					Defeated bosses offer a clue for the next recommended boss.
					You can re-summon some bosses you have already beaten, but most bosses drop all their loot on the first kill.
					You can place markers on your map — use them for gates you cannot open yet or bosses to come back to later.
					'''
				Heading10: Game Modes
				Page10:
					'''
					Unkindled: the default. Flasks, stamina on weapons, active shields and an extra accesory slot.
					Bearer of the Curse: everything above, plus an additional combat mechanic for each weapon class,
					20% more souls and a different stamina tempo, with stricter limits on healing & mana regen.
					Classic: vanilla healing, shields and magic, with no flask interface or stamina-based weapons.
					Left-click the Darksign to switch, and right-click it to read your class mechanic.				
					'''
				Heading11: Shields and Blocking
				Page11:
					'''
					Hold right mouse with a shield to raise it. It covers your front, above and below,
					but not your back. Harder hits and weaker shields use more stamina.
					Raise it just as a blow lands for a perfect parry: no damage, half the stamina, and it does stagger damage against melee attacks.
					Block any sooner than that and a little chip damage leaks through. Worse shields leak more.
					A heavy enough hit will break your guard outright, however much stamina you have.
					Greatshields leak nothing at all but are slower to recover. Bucklers are the opposite.
					'''
			}

			DodgerollMemo: {
				DisplayName: Dodgeroll Memo
				Tooltip:
					'''
					It looks like a diary entry. It reads as follows:
					"There have been rumours of bandits in the forest lately,
					so father has been apprehensive about letting me go into the
					forest alone to pick mushrooms... Pfft, what does he know?
					I may be small, but I'm nimble and have mastered [c/00ffd4:the technique]
					[c/00ffd4:of the dodgeroll!] I'll be fine as long as I don't run out of stamina..."
					Judging by how bandits were in possession of this note, I guess it
					didn't go too well for them. Perhaps I can make good use of this technique?
					'''
				RollKey: "[c/ffbf00:Press {0} to roll.]"
				RebindHint: "[c/ffbf00:You can change this key bind in Settings: Controls.]"
			}

