			EmeraldHerald: {
				DisplayName: Emerald Herald
				Name1: Jade
				FirstEncounter:
					'''
					Are you the one I was sent to warn? My name is Jade, I am not of this world. I was sent here to warn you of the dangers posed by Attraidies, the Mindflayer King.
					He has grown mighty in power and seeks to destroy not only your world, but also mine and many others.
					'''
				HasShard:
					'''
					Is that a shard you've found? Here, let me see it.
					So that I may help you. To see light, to see hope. No matter how faint it might be
					'''
				RewardTip: Listen to everything I have to say and I may give you a reward.
				AttraidiesTip: Seek misery. For misery will lead you to greater, stronger souls. You will never defeat Attraidies with a soul so frail and palid.
				Tip1: Forge your souls in the flames of sacred bonfires and make their power your own.
				Tip2: If you ever chance upon a weapon cursed by poor craftsmanship, bring it to me and I shall bless it.
				Tip3: I hope you have a keen eye, for this is a land brimming with secrets...
				Tip4: The frequent use of potions will prove vital on your journey, especially when attempting to retrieve lost souls.
				Tip5: A pickaxe or sticky bomb can be used to break blocks that are 1 width wide, but there are some exceptions. Stone gates need switches to open. If in doubt...
				Tip6: Dark souls have special properties. On death, you will drop all your souls and have one chance to recover them. Die before this and they are gone for good.
				Tip7: On your journey you will encounter unlit bonfires. Light them and enjoy the peaceful respite they provide. You can use them as checkpoints and for crafting with souls.
				Tip8: You can stash excess items in the bottomless Storage Slot to the right of your inventory. Press T to open. Shift-click to transfer items.
				Tip9: Stronger pickaxes can be used to open gates of strong ore.
				Tip10: And finally... I'm not sure what it means, but I was told to tell you to read something called the 'Game Manual' for more information. I get the feeling you know where to find it.
				ReceiveGift: Take this with you. May it ease your journey.
				Luck: Good luck.
				Gift: If you ever need more, you may roast some over the flames of a bonfire. Farewell.
				BotCGift: Bearer of the Curse, these lifegems and Starlight Shards will no doubt prove to be invaluable on your journey. Farewell.
				UnkindledGift: Unkindled one, your fire still smolders. Take these lifegems — may they sustain you on the road ahead. Farewell.
				EasterEgg: Bearer... Seek... Seek... Lest...
				button1: Bless
				button2v1: Seek knowledge...
				button2v2: Recieve gift
				button2v3: Give Shard
				button2v4: Receive tome
				TomeOffer: Before we speak, take this — a [c/6d8827:Boss Hunting Tome]. Hover over any boss in its pages to learn where it dwells, and re-summon those you have already slain.
				TomeGiven: May it guide your path. Now then, what knowledge do you seek?
				BringShards: If you happen to find another Restoration Flask Shard, bring it to me. So that I may ease your burden.
				EstusUpgrade: "Estus Flask size increased! Max charges: "
				CeruleanUpgrade: "Cerulean Flask size increased! Max charges: "

