			MiakodaNPC: {
				DisplayName: Miakoda
				Name1: Miakoda
				ButtonHelp: Help
				ButtonChat: Chat
				NextButtonExit: Exit
				NextButtonContinue: Continue
				Quote1:
					'''
					I was once the Spirit of the Moon, free, unshackled. Even though now I'm limited to this doll, my connections to the spirits and souls of old remain.
					If you ever need a helping hand on your journey, feel free to just ask. I can give you a couple of tips or guide you to where you need to go next.
					'''
				Quote2:
					'''
					These items you sometimes find {0}, that appear useless... don't be so quick to assume.
					If it can be crafted into something new with dark souls, it may be worth investigating its hidden potential.
					'''
				Quote3:
					'''
					Its been decades since I was sealed away into this little doll.
					I don't know how you humans live like this, trapped in the same shape day after day!
					If you have the dark souls to spare, I'd appreciate a change of pace!
					'''
				Quote4:
					'''
					Those Dark Souls that you so thoughtlessly collect; to Humans their power is a curse rather than a boon.
					While gathering them may grant you the power of old, using them consigns you to the same fate as those you slaughter.
					You too one day will become a Dark Soul. At that time my debt to you will be repaid.
					'''
				FullMoonForm:
					'''
					As a spirit of the Full Moon, I drink its light.
					Under the gaze of the Moon all wounds shall be healed.
					'''
				CrescentMoonForm:
					'''
					The moon... It shifts. Light warps into a cutting crescent.
					As an embodiment of the crescent, I shall guide its distortion to follow your blade.
					'''
				NewMoonForm:
					'''
					Empty, so empty. The moon yearns for what it cannot have.
					Fight quickly, for the moon will shield you in your time of need and devour that which is otherwise lost.
					With it, I shall fill your coffers.
					'''
				ArazSuspicion:
					'''
					That Wizard you found in the Wyvern Mage Fortress... I doubt the truth of his words.
					The Elemental Crests, they are a cornerstone to the natural magic that flows through the world.
					Why now are they inscribed with riddles, inscribed with human magic? Moreover how would their combination weaken the Mindflayer King?
					'''
				LunaticCultist:
					'''
					Have you seen that accursed man, that raving lunatic!?
					He shackled me into this doll just because I refused to serve that God of his...
					It calls itself The Moon Lord? Only in its dreams!
					'''
				BrotherNotRescued: I could sense an Aura similar to yours right after you freed me from Skeletron! {0}, you should go and find them in the depths of The Forgotten City.
				JungleWyvern:
					'''
					An ancient beast guards The Forgotten City. It holds a Ring that was enchanted with powerful revitalizing magic.
					Those who wear it are fabled to possess unending stamina and unparalleled grace! You should go and wield its powers for yourself.
					'''
				JungleWyvernBiomeHint:
					'''
					The Forgotten City is to the left and down from where you fought The First of the Dead, Skeletron.
					We should go there next and see what we can find.
					'''
				HMWifeNotRescued:
					'''
					...I see. Not only did that man slaughter your village, but he also imprisoned your wife!
					I dare not say what this might mean. {0}, you must ensure great caution in whatever you do.
					The MindFlayer King, his ambitions... They are truly darker than they appear on the surface.
					'''
				WifeRescuedPart1:
					'''
					That evil one, he manipulates you. Your old friend, Aaron, mind controlled and laced with the magic to unleash hell upon the world.
					Your brother, conveniently armed with the knowledge of your wife's survival.
					And your poor wife, who after enduring so much is able to tell you of the knowledge he so desperately sought.
					'''
				WifeRescuedPart2:
					'''
					Gather the crests, but do not offer them up to summon The Mindflayer King.
					The revenge you seek is not worth it!
					I fear of what may come if you keep playing into his schemes...
					'''
				WallofFleshBiomeHintPart1:
					'''
					Deep under the Forgotten City lies a land corrupted by the Flame of the Abyss, The Underworld.
					It is said that this is where the Witch of Izalith mistakenly created this evil that seeks to consume all.
					'''
				WallofFleshBiomeHintPart2:
					'''
					You wish murder on the betrayer, Aaron, yes? Find this land and offer up that Stone of Protection he so mockingly gave to you at an Altar somewhere deep within.
					He shall be butchered like a chicken by the Power of Chaos.
					'''
				WallofFleshJungleLeverHint: There should be another way up into The Forgotten City that opens the final gate from The Underworld.
				WallofFleshHellLeversHint:
					'''
					The Underworld is said to have been locked by the Knights of Gwyn after they drove back the Abyss.
					To get through, you must find the keys scattered throughout The Underworld. They will open the pathway to deeper within.
					'''
				SolidWallsHiddenPathsHint:
					'''
					Keep an eye out for hidden paths within the world. Most are adorned with Crystals - a consequence of the buried power accumulated within.
					However some mischievous spirits harvest the crystals for themselves and obscure the path with illusionary magic.
					They cannot fool a keen and courageous explorer. Walk up to any suspicious walls and press up against them - their magic will not withstand such a test.
					'''
				ProjectileHiddenPathsHintPart1:
					'''
					If you see a gate that isn't locked behind levers, switches, or key, do not fret! There might be another way!
					The most ancient of hidden paths were constructed by the people of Izalith.
					They lived underground and were known for their whimsical mastery of magic.
					'''
				ProjectileHiddenPathsHintPart2:
					'''
					Their tunnels were only accessible by striking a teal plate, usually hidden around a couple of corners or above the gate.
					They took pride in using controllable magic to access these paths, but a poorly hidden one could be struck by a mundane projectile too.
					'''
				BreakableBlocksHint:
					'''
					Your pickaxe is a useful tool, capable of tearing down thin walls with ease.
					There are certain materials however I think you could destroy without having to worry about thickness.
					Sand, Slush, and Transparent Ice should be easy to tunnel through freely.
					'''
				ShadowKeyHint:
					'''
					Certain chests require a certain kind of key, given only to those acknowledged by Skeletron, the first of the dead.
					While I was imprisoned by Skeletron, I overheard he left one Shadow Key deep below the Frozen Ocean.
					I have also heard rumors that the Wyvern Mage offers one to those who play a rather twisted game of his, hosted within his fortress atop the mountains to the East...
					'''
				HardmodeLorePart1:
					'''
					After you sliced through the wall that separated the mortal realm from the supernatural, 8 beings of great power awakened from their slumber.
					They have linked themselves to the elements, feeding on the world to grow ever stronger.
					'''
				HardmodeLorePart2:
					'''
					Their combined power burdens the First Flame, and if they remain awake this Era will soon be plunged into eternal darkness.
					You must find The Awakened, defeat them in battle, and gather their elemental crests. The remains hold the key to heal this shattered realm.
					'''
				3WingsLorePart1:
					'''
					Do you wish to know more about The Awakened? I will start with the first of the Awakened, the Three Wings.
					The Rage is the Legendary Phoenix, embodiment of Anger, Passion, and Fire. It possesses the Legendary Power of Rebirth. Even when slain, it will immediately begin the cycle of life renewed as an Egg.
					The Sorrow is the embodiment of Sadness, Despair, and Water. Not much is known about this Wing, except it is adorned by a golden hairpin that it protects with its life.
					'''
				3WingsLorePart2:
					'''
					The Hunter is the strongest of The Three Wings, embodiment of Pride and the Law of the Jungle. Its contempt pervades the world, limiting the ability of flight for all those it deems as prey.
					If any of them take enough damage, their natural defenses will activate. This will enrage them and increase the damage of all their attacks!
					Be cautious, all of them are formidable adversaries.
					'''
				3MachinesLorePart1:
					'''
					Do you wish to know more about The Awakened? I will now tell you of three more Awakened, the three Calamities.
					Made from the desecrated remains of an ancient Eldritch being, the Calamities invaded and nearly destroyed everything long ago.
					Woe it be to anyone living during that apocalyptic time.
					'''
				3MachinesLorePart2:
					'''
					The Destroyer is the first of the three, a planetary eater. It tunneled through the flesh of mother nature, consuming all but the corruption it left in its wake.
					This is the origin of the underground tunnels of the world today: scars left by this mighty destroyer. Sealed away into the Shadow Labyrinth by the Dragons, The Destroyer was used in their trials for coming of age.
					A trial of Fire, Water, Flight, and Might. Maybe this was the secret to the Legendary Might of the Dragons?
					'''
				3MachinesLorePart3:
					'''
					The Machine is the second of the three, a weapon of mass destruction. It rained fire and brimstone upon the land, slaughtering all who dared step foot on the surface.
					Many civilizations fell to this terrifying being of great evil. In their desperate hour the people of the Moon tribe cried out, and the Moon answered their pleas.
					The Machine was lured into their Temple of Worship and sealed away by a great rain from the heavens, flooding the temple and sealing the calamity away for good.
					'''
				3MachinesLorePart4:
					'''
					The Triad is the last of the three, the eyes of death. They searched out and exterminated the Heroes of old, leaving all without hope. Nowhere was safe, not even the underground.
					Even a mere glance could mean certain death. The Triad were the only of the three Calamities to be appeased, rather than defeated.
					Humanity built them a shrine of glass, so they could observe freely from their crystaline throne. It is said that they continue to watch us all to this very day.
					'''
				RageBiomeHint:
					'''
					Seek out the Hallowed Caverns. Using the Molten Pickaxe dropped by The Wall, break down the cobalt gates to the east.
					The spirits tell me The First of The Awakened, The Rage, has made that lair its den.
					'''
				RageEscapeHell:
					'''
					Well done {0}! Defeating that abomination had consequences, however. I can sense great magic penetrating this realm.
					No... This must have been a trap. Go to the east side of the underworld; you should be able to walk over the hell stone bridge now.
					I can feel our path leads us there.
					'''
				RageDeeperHint:
					'''
					The spirits of the cavern move through the Hallow, gathering beneath hidden depths to resist a formidable adversary.
					Go deeper into the Hallow. The Rage awaits beneath our feet.
					'''
				SorrowBiomeHintPart1:
					'''
					Our journey takes us further East. The next of the Awakened, The Sorrow, took nest deep below the Frozen Ocean.
					Unfortunately our way forward is currently barricaded.
					'''
				SorrowBiomeHintPart2:
					'''
					The Wyvern Mage, ally of the Mindflayer King, occupies a mountain fortress shrouded in invisible death that stands between us and the Eastern Ocean.
					The spirits can tell me no more. I fear this is a death trap, {0}... There must be another way through the mountain.
					'''
				SorrowEastHint:
					'''
					I underestimated you {0}! You made it past the secret magic of the Wyvern Mage and cleared a path towards the Frozen Ocean!
					All that is left is to head a little further east and dive deep beneath the waters: The Sorrow awaits us.
					'''
				RemixSorrowBiomeHintPart1:
					'''
					Our journey takes us further East. The next of the Awakened, The Sorrow, took nest deep below the Frozen Ocean.
					The gate after the ancestral spirit's lair is the way.
					'''
				RemixSorrowBiomeHintPart2:
					'''
					The Wyvern Mage, ally of the Mindflayer King, occupies a mountain fortress who guards the eastern skies.
					The spirits can tell me no more. I fear this is a death trap, {0}...
					'''
				SorrowDeeperHint: We should explore deep into the Ocean. I feel an icy power radiating within its depths.
				HunterBiomeHint:
					'''
					Beneath the burning sun, black smoke with a violet glow illuminates the path. Hearing that, I can only think of the tribe that once lived within the Western Desert.
					To get there, you must travel West past the Adamantine gates of the Corruption to seek their prior dwellings.
					'''
				HunterElengadRuinHint:
					'''
					The Orespeak built many traps underneath their tribe as a way to defend against the first coming of the Abyss.
					They were a tribe of Fire Walkers - they had the magical ability to walk on molten rock yet remain unharmed.
					If you don't have a way to cross lava, delving deep into their tunnels would be a fool's errand.
					'''
				HunterElengadRuinReady:
					'''
					With the ability to walk across Lava unscathed, you are now ready to delve into the Elengad Ruins and hunt the final wing of The Awakened, The Hunter.
					It will be dangerous {0}, be safe.
					'''
				FireWalkHint:
					'''
					It seems dangerous to explore the Elengad ruins now, {0}.
					You should explore further west and dive into the Nora Sea. Before it was washed away by a tidal storm, there used to be a town there.
					I'm sure Nora would bless an adventurer courageous enough to explore its depths with the ability to walk on Water and Fire like he did for the people who lived there long ago.
					'''
				RemixFireWalkHint:
					'''
					It seems dangerous to explore the Elengad ruins now, {0}.
					You should explore further west and explore the Tropics, or going back and clear the Scarlet Hill's blood demons.
					'''
				HunterClose:
					'''
					Keep going {0}, I can feel it, we are close! Be cautious however, The Hunter is the strongest of the three wings.
					I can feel the presence of another beast as well - it won't be alone.
					'''
				TempleOfSerris:
					'''
					The Hidden Temple of Serris...? I last heard about it from a brave soul who dared to delve deep into the Shadow Labyrinth.
					It is said that earning the recognition of Serris will grant one access to the depths of the Labyrinth.
					We don't need to go there yet, {0}. This path does not lead to the Hunter.
					'''
				RemixTempleOfSerris:
					'''
					Serris...? I last heard about it from a brave soul who dared to delve deep into the Basements of the Dark Tower.
					It is said that Serris, hidden below the tower, guards the access to a secret path somewhere.
					We don't need to go there yet, {0}. This path does not lead to the Hunter.
					'''
				DestroyerFromSerris:
					'''
					It is said that earning the recognition of Serris will grant one access to the depths of the Labyrinth.
					The path opened by defeating Serris-X should be somewhere under the Desert Surface, near the ruins.
					'''
				DestroyerFromHunter:
					'''
					A small sandy cave atop a hill... I'm sure we passed one before {0}, when we were traveling West from the corruption.
					This one seems easy!
					'''
				RemixDestroyerFromHunter:
					'''
					A small mushroom cave in the Mycelium Forest... I'm sure we passed one before {0}, when we were traveling West from the corruption. It was near the Truffle's home!
					This one seems easy!
					'''
				DestroyerLabrynthGates:
					'''
					The Shadow Labyrinth is full of gates that require using a switch, lever, or wall-mounted plate to pass through.
					The one who can navigate the Labyrinth is said to earn the right of awakening The Destroyer of Worlds.
					Unfortunately, it is now one of the awakened. You must destroy before our time runs out.
					'''
				DestroyerLabrynthSecretPaths:
					'''
					The spirits tell me of two hidden shortcuts within this Labyrinth, both shrouded in secrecy.
					The first is within an Ancient Greek Cave said to possess a golden mirror that protects against the Serpent's Gaze.
					The second is beyond a gate near the maw of the Labyrinth. It is guarded by both the Serpent and the Wraith of Shadow.
					'''
				DestroyerLabrynthLayout:
					'''
					The Shadow Labyrinth is said to contain three trials that test those who seek the Destroyer.
					The Trial of Fire, Water, and Flight. One must master all three before being deemed worthy of its presence.
					I can only imagine what lies deep within its depths, but I'm sure you can handle it {0}!
					'''
				MachineTempleLocationHint:
					'''
					Below a broken, familiar bridge huh. {0}, these riddles seem to be tailored to you personally.
					Maybe you should have a look around your Father's village. It's surely somewhere nearby.
					'''
				MachineTempleStraightForward:
					'''
					Discovering this temple was surely the hardest part. After beating the Shadow Temple, I'm sure this place will not pose any challenge!
					Go, {0}! The Machine awaits you in the depths!
					'''
				GolemJunglePyramidPlanteraHint:
					'''
					The spirits cry of a great evil emerging within the Jungle. It wishes for nothing but death.
					I do not know what manner of creature this is, but it must be stopped. Head to the east of where you first found your brother Elijah, within the Forgotten City.
					You will find a Pyramid dedicated to the Sun and Moon. It leeches from the power there.
					'''
				RemixGolemJunglePyramidPlanteraHint:
					'''
					The spirits cry of a great evil emerging within the Jungle. It wishes for nothing but death.
					I do not know what manner of creature this is, but it must be stopped. Do you remember the chlorophyte gate deep in the jungle, near the exit of the Volcano?
					You will find the path to the old jungle, where it draws its power from a powerful energy source.
					'''
				GolemJunglePyramidHint:
					'''
					Head to the east of where you first found your brother Elijah, within the Forgotten City.
					You will find a Pyramid dedicated to the Sun and Moon. That is the Pyramid you seek.
					'''
				RemixGolemJunglePyramidHint:
					'''
					Go back deep into the jungle and find the passage near the exit of the Meteor Temple.
					This is where you will find the Great Pyramid of Life, where this creature leeches its energy.
					'''
				GolemJungleMoonGate:
					'''
					On the way to the Pyramid, if an unbreakable gate seals your path do not fret. Use a cosmic watch to pass time until it is night.
					The light of the moon shall open your way forward.
					'''
				PlanteraLorePart1:
					'''
					Do you wish to know more about The Awakened? I will now tell you about Plantera, the Infection that plagues the Jungle.
					The Jungle is the heart of Mother Nature. When it was tunneled through by the Destroyer, the corruption it left behind could not consume the Jungle. However, its presence had other effects within.
					'''
				PlanteraLorePart2:
					'''
					It became a madness, a disease. Mother Nature could only contain the infection and keep it at bay.
					But Plantera, the incarnation of death and madness, will truly be freed one day. Its taint continues to spread throughout the Jungle whispering to those foolish enough to draw near.
					'''
				GolemLorePart1:
					'''
					Even Golem, once worshiped by as the Sun God, has fallen to the madness. He and his tribe of Lizardmen were once a shamanic tribe bound deeply to the Jungle.
					Envious of her power, Golem used the Jungle's magic long ago to usurp the Empress of Light. This linked his very existence with the Jungle.
					When the Jungle went mad, so did he and his people.
					'''
				GolemLorePart2:
					'''
					His last act while still sane was to seal himself away deep within his Temple.
					The sealing was said to be done in two parts. The lock was entrusted to the Moon Tribe, who resided in the present day Flooded Machine Temple.
					The key was linked to the very infection that drove them mad: Plantera itself. If the source of the madness could be destroyed, the key to their freedom would reveal itself.
					'''
				GolemEnter:
					'''
					The Golem temple is magically linked to the Jungle, Sun, and Moon. Enter the temple through the Jungle Pyramid and proceed with caution.
					The madness and malice emenating from this temple is unlike anything we've ever seen before, {0}.
					'''
				TriadLocationHint: Our path draws us now to the Legendary Watchers of old, the Triad. They should reside within their shrine upon the Twin Peaks of Arazium.
				TriadCaution: Be careful {0}. None who have dared to face the Triad have survived their gaze. It would be wise to become as strong as possible before seeking them out.
				TriadEmpressOfLight:
					'''
					The Triad are akin to Gods, far above ordinary mortals. To face them in battle and triumph might require the power of a true god.
					Have you ever looked up at the clouds floating above Ashen Peak Village? It is said that the Empress of Light resided there, before she was sealed away by the false God.
					She will be weakened by her long sealing - and even more so if she cannot draw power from the sun. You must plunder her might.
					'''
				AttraidesLocation:
					'''
					Well done {0}! You have defeated all the awakened and gathered their elemental crests. The first flame will continue to burn brightly for ages to come.
					Do not seek Attraides out in the Western Desert. He seeks to awaken an Ancient Evil with the World Essence you have gathered - do not make the mistake of offering it to him for revenge.
					'''
				ToShaman:
					'''
					{0}, an ancient evil invades this world. Killing Attraides has now unleashed the Abyss.
					Go to the western edge of the world and find the Shaman elder. He should know how to reseal the abyss.
					'''
				WaterFiendKrakenHint:
					'''
					We must first dive into the Great Chasm and find the Lizhard Gate that blocks the path to the Old One's Tree.
					According to the Shaman Elder, this is where the Water Fiend Kraken has made its dwelling.
					It is the first of the beings we need to slay before we can fight Gwyn, Keeper of the Flame.
					'''
				RemixWaterFiendKrakenHint:
					'''
					West of the Mycelium Forest near the Shadow Temple lies a path to the Dreamlike Caverns. 
					According to the Shaman Elder, this is where the Water Fiend Kraken has made its dwelling.
					It is the first of the beings we need to slay before we can fight Gwyn, Keeper of the Flame.
					'''
				FireFiendMarilithHint:
					'''
					East of the Elengad Ruins and Shadow temple lies a path to the Catacombs. 
					There lies the Herald of Chaos, Fire Fiend Marilith. 
					It is the second of the beings we must slay.
					'''
				RemixFireFiendMarilithHint:
					'''
					The burning path starts from inside hell below the Forgotten City. The spirits tell me of a forgotten passage entombed in molten rock.
					There lies the Herald of Chaos, Fire Fiend Marilith. 
					It is the second of the beings we must slay.
					'''
				EarthFiendLichHint1:
					'''
					Our fate calls us to the Western Edge of the World, deep into Hell. I can sense two paths leading to our destination.
					The first has us delving deep into the Western Ocean and diving through the magma that blocks our path.
					Past the spider's cave and through the hidden veil of Humanity's past, it is there.
					'''
				EarthFiendLichHint2:
					'''
					The second path starts from inside hell below the Forgotten City. The spirits tell me of a forgotten passage entombed in molten rock.
					Take that passage and travel a long ways west from it, until you reach the hidden veil of humanity's past.
					The Earth Fiend Lich will be near.
					'''
				RemixEarthFiendLichHint1:
					'''
					We must dive into the Great Chasm and find the Lihzahrd Gate that blocks the path to the Catacombs.
					Despite the horror of this place, we have no choice but to venture there and face what is there.
					The Earth Fiend Lich is here, deep in the Catacombs.
					'''
				SeathTheScalelessHint:
					'''
					Do you remember where you last fought The Sorrow? Deep within the frozen ocean lies the Betrayer of the Dragons, Seath the Scaleless.
					With the shackles of the world now shattered, Seath shall take flight in the Eastern Skies once more.
					If you defeat Seath and plunder his wings, you will become untouchable underneath the sky.
					'''
				WitchkingHint:
					'''
					The Spirits tell me of another, a being that instead of escaping the Abyss has made it his dwelling: The Witchking.
					He is not linked to Gwyn, but he holds the key to an old enemy of ours. Bring a blade that has the power to shatter magical wards.
					East of the hidden veil of Humanity's past within the Ashen Caves of the Abyss is where you'll find him. 
					'''
				RemixWitchkingHint:
					'''
					The Spirits tell me of another, a being that instead of escaping the Abyss has made it his dwelling: The Witchking.
					He is not linked to Gwyn, but he holds the key to an old enemy of ours. Bring a blade that has the power to shatter magical wards.
					East of the hidden veil of Humanity's past in Morgul Feleg, the depths of shadows that you'll find him. 
					'''
				WyvernMageShadowHint:
					'''
					{0}, I sensed a pulse of forbidden magic from that Sapphire you got from The Witchking. The Wyvern Mage is... Not dead. 
					Go to his fortress again and see what you can find. He must be killed for good if we are to ever face Gwyn in combat.
					'''
				WyvernMageNotKilledHint:
					'''
					The Wyvern Mage, prior ally of the Mindflayer King, occupies a mountain fortress shrouded in invisible death.
					There is a magic linking this Sapphire to somewhere within his fortress. Our path leads us there.
					'''
				ArtoriasHint:
					'''
					The Knight of Izalith, now turned puppet of the abyss: Artorias, is the being we need to fight next.
					Head over to the Forgotten City and seek out the Junction between it and the Jungle Pyramid.
					There lies his resting place.
					'''
				RemixArtoriasHint:
					'''
					The Knight of Izalith, now turned puppet of the abyss: Artorias, is the being we need to fight next.
					He rests to the Forgotten City at the Junction between it and the Undergrowth.
					But the Path through the ruins seems to be blocked, we need to find another way.
					The spirits tell me that the Great Foundry is the only way in: the entrance is located under a bridge on the surface of the jungle.
					'''
				ChaosHint:
					'''
					That Amethyst that we got from Artorias; it is a seal that locks away the throne of the King of Hell, Chaos. 
					Like the Calamities that came before it, this being's power and magic were too great for the world.
					He was sealed by the power of the moon. If you wish to face it in combat, head East from the Jungle Pyramid.
					'''
				RemixChaosHint:
					'''
					That Amethyst that we got from Artorias; it is a seal that locks away the throne of the King of Hell, Chaos. 
					Like the Calamities that came before it, this being's power and magic were too great for the world.
					He was sealed by the luminous power of the Hallow. If you wish to face it in combat, return at the entrance of the Hallowed Caves, now invaded by shadows.
					'''
				BlightHint:
					'''
					Should you decide to journey East again {0}, seek the far reaches of the frozen ocean. 
					There is a manifestation there, an infinitesimally small part of a higher being that seeks to widen the crack and fully enter our world..
					It is a Blight on the world. If it one day makes it through I fe our realm will be shattered.
					'''
				AbysmalOolacileSorcerer:
					'''
					Underneath the golem temple lies a Sorcerer, a being that holds a ring of great magic and vitality. 
					If you wish to claim its ring for yourself {0}, I'm sure the ring would greatly boost your magical capabilities.
					'''
				RemixAbysmalOolacileSorcerer:
					'''
					It seems that in the Frozen Cathedral also lies a powerful Sorcerer from Oolacile, a being that holds a ring of great magic and vitality. 
					If you wish to claim its ring for yourself {0}, I'm sure the ring would greatly boost your magical capabilities.
					'''
				DarkCloudHint:
					'''
					That mirror you hold... Do not look into it. That is an cursed artifact of the moon - one that manifests a future version of its beholder and twists it.
					An ordinary man might see himself turned into a serial killer, dangerous but not certainly deadly.
					For you {0}? You should know best how much untapped potential still lies within you. Looking into the mirror might just garuntee your undoing.
					'''
				RemixDarkCloudHint:
					'''
					That mirror you hold... Do not look into it. That is an cursed artifact of the Abyss - one that transports you 
					deep in the Abyss and manifests a future version of its beholder and twists it.
					An ordinary man might see himself turned into a serial killer, dangerous but not certainly deadly.
					For you {0}? You should know best how much untapped potential still lies within you. Looking into the mirror might just garuntee your undoing.
					'''
				GwynHint:
					'''
					You are ready to face Gwyn, keeper of the Flame and King of the Abyss. The beings that once supplied him with power are no more, vanquished by your hand.  
					He is the last of the Abyss. His death will allow you to become the next keeper of the flame and close the portal of the Abyss.
					Seek out his Tomb hidden somewhere within the Western Ocean. I believe in you, {0}.
					'''
				CannotHelp: You have done well, {0}, I have no more advice to offer you.
				ExhaustedDialogue: I believe we've talked enough {0}, I can't think of anything more to say for now.
			}

			ShamanElder: {
				DisplayName: Shaman Elder
				Name1: Alo
				Name2: Dakota
				Name3: Esadowa
				Name4: Kai
				Name5: Koda
				Name6: Lonato
				Name7: Micah
				Name8: Taregan
				Quote1:
					'''
					Man and animal once lived in harmony, until one day a particular tribe grew a sickness of the mind. 
					This tribe, known as the Takers, came to dominate the world, exterminating all other ways of being...
					'''
				Quote2: Arapaho once told me that all plants are our brothers and sisters. They talk to us and if we listen, we can hear them.
				Quote3: I am an animist, like the indigenous tribe who once lived in these lands were, before they were wiped out by the Takers.
				Quote4Part1: "You must never forget "
				Quote4Part2: ", you are not separate from nature. You are one with the whole universe."
				Quote5Part1: "The world is not a pyramid, "
				Quote5Part2: ", nor is man the top of it. The world is a web, and every strand of the web is connected."
				Quote6: Civilized man has grown a great sickness of the mind -- thinks he is superior to all creation. Thinks the world was made for him!
				Quote7: Apache said it is better to have less thunder in the mouth and more lightning in the hand.
				Quote8: Tuscarora once said they are not dead who live in the hearts they leave behind.
				PreAttraidies1: "[c/ffbf00:If you are able to defeat Attraidies, come and find me at my home beyond the Western Sea.] I will have something for you..."
				PreAttraidies2: "[c/ffbf00:In some time I will leave Ashen Peak and return to my home beyond the Western Sea.] Come find me there..."
				button2v1: Ask about The Abyss
				button2v2: Continue...
				AdvModeSHMQuote1:
					'''
					Red, it is as I feared. By killing Attraidies, a portal from
					the Abyss was opened, unleashing even more oppressive forces upon the world.
					The ancestors tell me that the portal can be closed, but
					you must first defeat the 3 Elemental Fiends: one of
					[c/2f8ee0:Water], one of [c/fcff00:Earth], and one of [c/f53d0a:Fire].
					You must also defeat 4 more lords of the Abyss:
					[c/ffbf00:Artorias], [c/00ffd4:Blight], [c/aa00ff:The Wyvern Mage Shadow], and [c/18ffe2:Seath the Scaleless].
					'''
				AdvModeSHMQuote2:
					'''
					My heart despairs for you, Red. It will not be easy. But if you succeed, you will have the strength
					to face the final lord, who has tended the flame of the Abyss since the world began.
					To the ancestors, he was known as [c/ff6618:Gwyn, Lord of Cinder].
					Gwyn's old tomb is buried somewhere beneath the Western sea, but he will surely kill you
					if you have not yet gathered the strength obtained from the other lords of the Abyss.
					'''
				RemixAdvModeSHMQuote2:
					'''
					My heart despairs for you, Red. It will not be easy. But if you succeed, you will have the strength
					to face the final lord, who has tended the flame of the Abyss since the world began.
					To the ancestors, he was known as [c/ff6618:Gwyn, Lord of Cinder].
					Gwyn's old tomb is buried somewhere in the Eternal Reef, but he will surely kill you
					if you have not yet gathered the strength obtained from the other lords of the Abyss.
					'''
				AdvModeSHMQuote3:
					'''
					Have you seen the [c/ffbf00:Lihzahrd Gates] scattered across this world? They will lead you towards your goal.
					I would start with the one deep inside the Great Chasm, which leads to the Old One's Tree.
					There is another, to the East of Elengad's Desert Ruins. The rest, I'm sure you will find. The ancestors will help guide you.
					'''
				RemixAdvModeSHMQuote3:
					'''
					Have you seen the [c/ffbf00:Lihzahrd Gates] scattered across this world? They will lead you towards your goal.
					I would start with the one at the very west of the Mycelium Forest, which leads to the Dreamlike Caverns.
					There is another, in a strange ship in the underworld. The rest, I'm sure you will find. The ancestors will help guide you.
					'''
				AdvModeSHMQuote4:
					'''
					There is one thing you should know about [c/ffbf00:Artorias], and another dark being that now stalks these lands,
					known as the [c/383838:Witchking].
					Both The Witchking and Artorias are protected by dark spells, making them practically invincible, but I have heard that
					[c/f53d0a:Fire Fiend Marilith] and certain [c/cffffa:Phantoms] that roam the skies are rumored to carry blades of fierce magic.
					[c/fcff00:The Barrow Blade] may just be strong enough to shatter their protection...
					'''
				RemixAdvModeSHMQuoteCHAOS:
					'''
					One last thing: Chaos's prison in the Hallow is cracked, and its darkness is spreading throughout the caves. 
					Because of this, some barriers have been activated and some passages are blocked. There is only one way back to Chaos in the Hallow; 
					[c/ffbf00:return to the starting point at the entrance to the Hallowed Caves, and you will find the path.]
					'''
				AdvModeSHMQuote5: Good luck, Red.
				SandboxSHMQuote1:
					'''
					To close the seal to the Abyss, you must defeat the 5 lords of The Abyss:
					[c/ffbf00:Artorias], [c/00ffd4:The Blight], [c/aa00ff:The Wyvern Mage Shadow],
					[c/fcff00:Chaos], and [c/18ffe2:Seath the Scaleless].
					With a lord soul from each of these beings you will be able to summon the final lord -
					[c/ff6618:Gwyn, Lord of Cinder].
					'''
				SandboxSHMQuote2:
					'''
					To craft the summoning item for each
					lord, you will need to return to eight familiar places
					and collect a unique item from an enemy you will find there:
					[c/424bf5:The Western Ocean], [c/888888:The Underground], [c/b942f5:The Corruption],
					[c/42f56c:The Jungle], [c/6642f5:The Dungeon], [c/eb4034:The Underworld], and [c/42f2f5:The Eastern Ocean].
					'''
				SandboxSHMQuote3:
					'''
					Defeating [c/ffbf00:Artorias], however, will not be possible without a little knowledge.
					To find him, you must seek out the [c/383838:Witchking] and restore the dark ring he drops.
					He will sometimes appear at night, and more often deeper\nunderground, especially in dungeons.
					The most assured way to find him, however, is to enter the Abyss yourself using the Covanent of Artorias ring.
					'''
				SandboxSHMQuote4:
					'''
					Both The [c/383838:Witchking] and [c/ffbf00:Artorias] are protected by dark spells, but I have heard that
					[c/cffffa:Fire Fiend Marilith] and certain [c/cffffa:Phantoms] that roam the skies are rumored to carry blades of fierce magic.
					Such a blade may just be strong enough to shatter their protection...
					'''

